Reject CPU random sampling with edge ids when the graph has none.

Compact topologies intentionally omit edge ids. A caller requesting sampled edge ids
would otherwise pass a null pointer into the CPU row-wise sampler and crash the process.
Reject that request at the native entry point; ordinary neighbor sampling is unchanged.

diff --git a/graphlearn_torch/csrc/cpu/random_sampler.cc b/graphlearn_torch/csrc/cpu/random_sampler.cc
--- a/graphlearn_torch/csrc/cpu/random_sampler.cc
+++ b/graphlearn_torch/csrc/cpu/random_sampler.cc
@@ -155,7 +155,10 @@ CPURandomSampler::SampleWithEdge(const torch::Tensor& nodes, int32_t req_num) {
   int64_t bs = nodes.size(0);
   const auto row_ptr = graph_->GetRowPtr();
   const auto col_idx = graph_->GetColIdx();
   const auto edge_ids = graph_->GetEdgeId();
+  TORCH_CHECK(edge_ids != nullptr,
+              "CPURandomSampler::SampleWithEdge requires edge ids; initialize the graph "
+              "with edge ids or call sample() when edge ids are not needed");
   const auto row_count = graph_->GetRowCount();

   torch::Tensor nbrs_num = torch::empty(bs, nodes.options());
